From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:18:12 -0500
Subject: fix: show what Arc holds before the bar imports it, and mend the
 import command

The command bar's "Import from Arc" imported at once and said nothing, so a person
could not see what was about to arrive or leave anything out. It now opens the
welcome flow's import step, with the summary, the boxes and the button.

Chromium's own import command, in the Bookmarks menu and the Mac's File menu,
opened Chromium's dialog through the People section. Settings hides that section,
so the command opened Settings and no dialog. It now opens the same step, which
offers all that dialog did and the other browsers.

Dia and Safari's export need no rows of their own: Settings' and the command bar's
"Import from another browser" already open their blocks, and a test now says so.

Why: import I4, I32, I41, I45 (BACKLOG S-101; docs/history/plan-2026-09-26.md
WEB-12, WEB-17, WEB-F4).
Removable when: the welcome flow's import step leaves the series.
